  "answer_text": "Because **Catherine McCoy** (sometimes spelled **Katherine McCoy**) can refer to a few notable real-life individuals and a fictional character, the correct identity depends on the context of your query:\n\n### 1. Katherine McCoy (American Graphic Designer & Educator)\nIf you are looking for a prominent figure in the world of design, you are likely referring to **Katherine McCoy** (born 1945). \n* **Who she is:** She is a highly influential American graphic designer, design theorist, and educator.\n* **Claim to Fame:** She is best known for co-chairing the graduate Design program at the prestigious **Cranbrook Academy of Art** from 1971 to 1995 alongside her husband, Michael McCoy. Under their leadership, the program became a pioneering hub for postmodern design, deconstructivism, and experimental design education. \n* **Key Achievements:** She was the first female president of the Industrial Designers Society of America (IDSA), a vice-president of the American Institute of Graphic Arts (AIGA), and she received the prestigious AIGA Medal in 1999 for her contributions to design and education.\n\n### 2. Catherine McCoy (Fictional Character in Literature)\nIf you are reading or researching historical fiction, she is a central character in the 2022 novel ***Beautiful Little Fools* by Jillian Cantor**.\n* **Who she is:** In this feminist retelling and reimagining of F. Scott Fitzgerald\u2019s *The Great Gatsby*, Catherine McCoy is the sister of Myrtle Wilson (a character briefly known simply as \"Catherine\" in the original classic). \n* **In the Book:** Cantor expands her role significantly, portraying Catherine McCoy as a passionate suffragette fighting for women's independence and trying to protect her sister from an abusive marriage in the years leading up to the fateful summer of 1922.\n\n### 3. Dr. Kathleen \"Kathy\" McCoy (Immunologist & Microbiome Researcher)\nIf you are looking at scientific or medical research, she is a world-renowned researcher.\n* **Who she is:** Dr. Kathy McCoy is a professor in the Department of Physiology and Pharmacology at the University of Calgary\u2019s Cumming School of Medicine. \n* **Claim to Fame:** She is the Scientific Director of the International Microbiome Centre. Her research focuses on immunology and the gut microbiome\u2014specifically how exposure to microbes early in life regulates the immune system and impacts susceptibility to diseases like allergies, autoimmune disorders, and cancer.\n\n### 4. Catherine McCoy (Naturopath & Wellness Practitioner)\nIf you are looking into alternative medicine or health coaching, she is an Australian integrative naturopath.\n* **Who she is:** Catherine McCoy is the founder of the **iNaturally Clinic** based in Canberra, Australia.\n* **Claim to Fame:** She is a writer, presenter, and wellness practitioner with over 20 years of experience specializing in fatigue solutions, metabolic health, and women's wellness.",
